  "id": "bumba_meu_boi_maranhao",
  "name": "Bumba-meu-boi do Maranhão (São Luís ox drama)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Ox-drama festivity of Maranhão performed in the June festival cycle around the feasts of São João, São Pedro and São Marçal, enacting the death and resurrection of a prized ox; it is registered as Brazilian cultural heritage by IPHAN and inscribed on the UNESCO Representative List. Groups are classed by sotaque (matraca, zabumba, orquestra, baixada and costa-de-mão), each with its own percussion and toada style. The cards follow the matraca sotaque of São Luís island, whose hardwood matraca blocks, large fire-tuned pandeirões and tambor-onça friction drum carry the toadas: palitos stand in for the matracas, a source-unspecified pandero for the pandeirões and a source-unspecified shaker for the amo's maracá.",
  "recipe": "classic modern bumba-meu-boi do maranhão, groove Percussion, Brazilian branch. palitos, pandero source shaker source unspecified. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
